 ## Overview
-Visible Block Faces is a voxel surface extraction method that generates a single quad for every visible face of a voxel block, culling faces where the neighbor is solid [S1, S3, S4]. It solves the problem of redundant geometry generation by removing hidden faces between adjacent opaque full cubes [S2]. Unlike [Greedy Meshing](3674-gpu-marching-cubes-face-based.md), which merges adjacent coplanar faces into larger rectangles, Visible Block Faces produces suboptimal but quickly generated meshes with minimal computational overhead [S3, S4]. It builds on [Voxel Chunk Meshing with Culling](2523-voxel-chunk-meshing-with-culling.md) by implementing the culling logic directly during mesh generation rather than as a post-processing step.
